#!/bin/bash
# land-first-stone-first.sh — the stones get a buying order, the sheet's
# proportions get fixed against the reference, and the remedies page gives one
# practice a week instead of six at once.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# PRECONDITION: land-gem-sheets.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="Which one do I buy first"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"A price per carat is not a price"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-gem-sheets.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="92bef7cbd61953220c06f10187b121b35a8be3d1ccf69de9624092ea00471d57"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-stone-answer.test.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
Which one do I buy first

THE STONES ARE RANKED NOW. Four sheets with no order is a page that did the hard
part and stopped one step short — the tradition is not neutral between them. 1
is the must-have, and the sheet says outright what that means: if you wear only
one stone, wear this one. 2 is worn alongside it and never instead of it. After
that it is addition.

The rank comes from the POSITION, not the role, and that distinction is the
whole reason it is computed on the server. Without a birth time there is no life
stone and the moon rashi's stone leads — on that page it is genuinely the
must-have, not the fourth item on a list with three holes in it.

It also gives the reference's numbered badge something true to say. The
catalogue numbers each card 1 to 30; on a personalised page that is answering a
question nobody asked. It carries the buying order instead.

Where the wearing table says two planets are allies, the sheet says the stones
are traditionally worn together. It never says the opposite: the enmity list is
a file we do not have, so a stone missing from that line is not being called
incompatible — it is not being claimed either way.

THREE THINGS THE RENDER FOUND, AND ONLY THE RENDER COULD HAVE.

  The sheet was 640px wide when it should be 520. This application has no
  global `box-sizing: border-box`, so a max-width is a CONTENT width — 560 plus
  80 of padding. The arc stretched to 560 against a 250px stone, the curve
  flattened, and the trait words read as floating above the photograph instead
  of arched over it. The reference's proportion is arc = 1.96 x the stone and it
  only holds if that number is the inner one.

  The stones were being squashed. The <img> carries width=250 height=220 so the
  box is reserved before the picture lands, and without `width/height: auto`
  those attributes also SIZE it — a square stone rendered 250x220. Thirty pixels,
  invisible on a ruby, obvious on a pearl.

  And the arc took three goes: at 100% width the words float, capped at the
  viewBox an inline <svg> tucks up beside the role capsule, and text longer than
  its path is clipped rather than wrapped. It is a block, the pull is -25% so it
  survives a resize, and the type is sized for the longest trait line in the
  catalogue rather than for the ruby's.

ONE PRACTICE A WEEK, ON THE REMEDIES PAGE. It listed six at once: six cards,
equal weight, each a small worthwhile thing to do. Nobody does six things. A
list that long is read as a menu, and a menu of self-improvement is a menu
people close. These are practices — they work by being repeated — so the page
names the one that is yours between Monday and Sunday, dated, and lets the rest
wait.

The week does the choosing. The index is whole weeks since the epoch, modulo the
list: the same practice every time you open the page for seven days, turning
over on its own overnight on Monday, working through every practice before it
repeats. Nothing is stored, so the same arithmetic gives the same answer on
every device and after every deploy — which a random pick or a saved cursor
would not. It turns over where the citizen is, not in UTC, and it rotates only
through the practices that survived the health filter, because a rotation with a
hole in it shows an empty week.

The rest are still there and still dated. Hiding them would make the page feel
thinner than it is, and seeing next Monday's practice is what makes this week's
read as a turn rather than a fragment.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: Which one do I buy first
 Both sides — push, then give Railway a minute before opening
 Astrology -> Gemstones and Astrology -> Remedies.
===============================================================

DONE
